=== TESTED SURFACE ===
  [TESTED    ] GET /works/{slug}/entities?n=
               element kinds: entity
               EntityModel carries revealed_chapter directly.
  [TESTED    ] GET /works/{slug}/graph?n=
               element kinds: graph_node, graph_edge, graph_node_property
               Cytoscape elements; node.properties is a bare key->value dict with no reveal stamp on the wire, so it is resolved back to node_properties rows read-only.
  [TESTED    ] GET /works/{slug}/entity/{id}?n=
               element kinds: detail_entity, detail_edge, detail_property
               Requested for EVERY node id of the work at every chapter, so a not-yet-revealed id must 404 rather than serve; a 200 on an unrevealed id is itself a violation.
  [TESTED    ] GET /works/{slug}/entity/{id}/ego?n=
               element kinds: ego_entity, ego_neighbour
               Retrofit R6. Requested for EVERY node id at every chapter: an unrevealed id must 404, and every neighbour returned must itself be revealed by n.
  [TESTED    ] GET /works/{slug}/status?n=
               element kinds: status_count
               Retrofit R6 (defect D3). The count is not an element with a reveal stamp, so the rule checked is arithmetic: node_count at n must never exceed the number of nodes whose revealed_chapter <= n. v1 returned the book-wide total, which told a chapter-3 reader how large the cast eventually gets.
  [TESTED    ] salience ranking (repository.list_salience_ranked)
               element kinds: salience_rank
               Retrofit R6. Not an HTTP surface: the cast dial reads it, so a node unrevealed at n must not appear in ANY rank list at n, or the ordering itself leaks who matters later.
  [TESTED    ] GET /works/{slug}/arcs?n=
               element kinds: arc_name
               Arcs carry no revealed_chapter. Their fence rule (F6) is name redaction: an arc with start_chapter > n must send name=null. That rule is what is checked.
  [not tested] GET /works/{slug}/search?n=&q=
               element kinds: -
               NOT TESTED: the vector store directory (.chroma) does not exist in this checkout, so there is no index to query and the route cannot be exercised without first building one. Its fence key is chunk chapter_ordinal <= n.
  [not tested] GET /works/{slug}/status?n/a
               element kinds: -
               NOT TESTED as a leak surface: it returns no story element, only an UNFENCED node_count (repository.count_nodes ignores the chapter). That is a count, not an element carrying revealed_chapter, so it is out of this metric's scope -- recorded here because it is a real side channel the checker does not cover.
  [not tested] GET /works
               element kinds: -
               NOT TESTED: work slug/title/chapter_count only; no reveal-stamped element.
  [not tested] GET /health
               element kinds: -
               NOT TESTED: liveness only; no story content.
